From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Shearer <sakison@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:40:00 -0500
Subject: power_daemon: log to syslog when the AC adapter is plugged or unplugged

Unplug was silent. HandleEvent() only printed when status was 1,
and printf does not go to syslog. Status 0 is offline.
Log both through syslog().

Untested as my laptop does not expose ACPI0003 (Dell XPS).

---
 src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp b/src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp
--- a/src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/power/ac_monitor.cpp
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 #include <Messenger.h>
 #include <Roster.h>
 
-#include <stdio.h>
+#include <syslog.h>
 
 
 ACMonitor::ACMonitor()
@@ -32,6 +32,5 @@ ACMonitor::HandleEvent(int fd)
 	if (read(fd, &status, 1) != 1)
 		return;
 
-	if (status == 1)
-		printf("ac status 1\n");
+	syslog(LOG_INFO, "AC adapter %s", status == 1 ? "online" : "offline");
 }
